KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ forwarding-ref accepts a const enum lvalue: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG: must fail: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/3: a forwarding reference `T&&` deduces T as "lvalue
reference to A" from an lvalue argument of type A, for any A including an
enumeration.  CBMC wrongly rejects the call ("found no match" -> CONVERSION
ERROR) when the argument is a const-qualified ENUM lvalue; a const scalar or a
non-const enum resolves fine, so the defect is specific to deducing/binding a
forwarding reference from a const enum argument (the deduced `const E&`
parameter is dropped during overload resolution).  Surfaced (with the
separately-fixed heterogeneous-pack defect cpp11_variadic_fwd_ref_heterogeneous)
by src/util/validate_expressions.cpp's `call_on_expr<...>(ns, vm)`, which
forwards a `const validation_modet` (enum class).  Flip to CORE once fixed.
